          "freshSource": "Jo will collect three comments after a Wednesday pilot. Rene will update the instructions. The continuation decision date is unset.",
          "example": "<p>Imagine asking someone to “organise a great event.” They would need to guess what matters to you. A smaller request is easier to check: “Draft a plan using these people and this time. Leave undecided details open.”</p>\n<p>A useful starting task has three parts:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Source:</strong> information you can point to.</li>\n<li><strong>Draft:</strong> one useful thing to produce.</li>\n<li><strong>Check:</strong> something observable that would make you keep or change it.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>The draft may suggest a new idea. It must identify that idea as a suggestion rather than turn it into an agreed fact.</p>\n<h4>Work — organise meeting actions</h4>\n<p><strong>Source W1:</strong> A team will test a new process next Tuesday. Sam will write the checklist. Alex will gather feedback. No announcement owner or date is recorded.</p>\n<p><strong>Worked task:</strong> Draft an action table from the notes. I will compare each task, owner and date with the note. A missing owner or date stays “not specified.”</p>\n<p>Next Tuesday is the process test date. It is not automatically a deadline for every other action.</p>",
