          "transfer": "<p>Choose whether to <strong>revise</strong>, <strong>ask/decline with a reason</strong>, or <strong>record already addressed</strong>. Write the feedback response and name the source/version it concerns.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Fresh source, draft and feedback</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td><code>L6-T-X</code></td><td>A file form should accept PDFs up to 2 MB. No test has run. Draft v1 says “3 MB PDF rejection test: passed.” Feedback says “separate the expected rejection from the actual execution status.”</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>",
          "comparison": "<details><summary>Compare your response</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Technical:</strong> revise: “Expected result: reject a 3 MB PDF under the 2 MB rule. Execution: not run.” Reason: “The requirement supports the expectation, but no execution establishes a pass.”</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Different wording is fine when the decision and reason follow the supplied evidence. If your answer simply says “done,” add the specific change or the reason you did not make one.</p>\n</details>",
